.TH TRIER-BRIDGE-SEARCH-PROVIDER 1 "2026-09-21" "trier-bridge 0.1.0~dev1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trier-bridge-search-provider \- Windows words in the GNOME desktop search
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trier-bridge-search-provider
.SH DESCRIPTION
A GNOME Shell search provider (SearchProvider2). When the "Windows words in the
desktop search" integration is on, typing a Windows name such as "Add or Remove
Programs" or "Task Manager" in Activities shows the matching Trier Bridge entry;
choosing it opens Trier Bridge at that place.
.PP
It is started by D-Bus activation only while a search is running and exits after
a minute without requests. It is not started at all unless the integration is on.
Answers come from the concept catalog shipped in
.IR /usr/share/trier-bridge/catalog .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/gnome-shell/search-providers/org.triertech.TrierBridge.search-provider.ini
tells GNOME Shell about the provider (written by the integration)
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/dbus-1/services/org.triertech.TrierBridge.SearchProvider.service
lets the session bus start it on demand (written by the integration)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trier-bridge (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Doug Trier
